## Things to Avoid

<!--
  THE HIGHEST-VALUE SECTION. Also the most-skipped. Do not leave this
  as placeholder text — a specific, opinionated list here is what
  actually constrains agent action.

  Aim for 5-12 concrete entries. Each entry names a specific pattern,
  file, or command and a specific reason to avoid it. Generic entries
  ("don't write bad code") are worse than nothing.
-->

- **Do not modify `src/generated/`** (or the equivalent for {{stack}}) — files are auto-generated by [tool]. Regenerate instead of edit.
- **Do not add `console.log` / `System.out.println` / `print()`** to production code — use the logger with a structured message. Debug prints reach production and pollute logs.
- **Do not use wall-clock time** (`Date.now`, `LocalDateTime.now`, `datetime.now()`) directly. Inject a `Clock` (or equivalent) so tests stay deterministic. See docs/TESTING.md.
- **Do not use `assertTrue(x.equals(y))`** in tests — prefer `assertThat(x).isEqualTo(y)` / `expect(x).toEqual(y)` for readable-diff failure messages.
- **Do not commit anything to `.env`** — only `.env.example` / `.env.sample`. Secrets never leave a secrets manager.
- **Do not add dependencies without a justification comment** in the manifest (package.json / pom.xml / pyproject.toml). Every added dep is future maintenance surface.
- **[add project-specific gotchas here — deprecated APIs, migration in flight, known flaky areas]**

## Agent Governance

<!--
  The advisory half of the two-layer governance pattern (see rubric
  §Part 1 D03 and §Part 2 A03). What the agent must not do (do-not-modify),
  what it must always do (always-run), and when it should hand off to
  a human (escalate-when). The enforced half lives in .claude/settings.json.

  Every entry here should have a matching enforcement in settings.json
  where possible. Advisory rules with no enforcement are legitimate but
  should be annotated explicitly ("advisory-only, intentionally not enforced").
-->

### Do not modify

- `src/generated/` — auto-generated by [tool]; regenerate rather than edit
- `db/migrations/` — migrations already applied to production; new changes go in a new migration file
- `.github/workflows/` — CI configuration requires human review before merge

### Always run before committing

- `ai-native-verify .` — deterministic AI-native compliance check
- `[test command]` — full test suite
- `[lint command]` — linter
- `pre-commit run --all-files` — pre-commit hooks (also runs automatically on `git commit`)

### Escalate to a human when

- Modifying authentication, authorization, or session handling logic
- Adding or changing database migrations
- Changing API contracts (request/response shapes, endpoint paths, response codes)
- Any change touching more than [N] files in a single task
- Any change to `.claude/settings.json`, `.github/workflows/`, or `.mcp.json` (policy changes)
- Any dependency addition that introduces a new production runtime requirement
